% Infrared Heating Pad Systems: LCD L33825 and its Policy Article A52477
% (DME MACs), which apply NCD 270.6 (Infrared Therapy Devices). A policy
% program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery,
% benefit category, continued need, refills) and decides the claims for the
% infrared heating pad system (E0221) and its replacement pads (A4639). The
% LCD states no coverage criterion: "there are no indications for which these
% devices have been demonstrated to have any therapeutic effect. The device
% and any related accessories will be denied as not medically reasonable and
% necessary." So this policy CONCLUDES NOTHING: no claim it decides is
% reasonable and necessary, and a claim for its codes fails at the question.
% The codes are in scope and in the durable medical equipment benefit — the
% Policy Article says the systems "are considered for coverage under the
% Durable Medical Equipment benefit" while the NCD precludes payment — and
% denied there. The NCD's text is not among the sources of this directory:
% the LCD's statement of it is what is cited.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base infrared_heating includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base infrared_heating includes:

LCD L33825 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33825".
the text of LCD L33825 is at "sources/lcd/L33825.txt".
Policy Article A52477 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52477".
the text of Policy Article A52477 is at "sources/article/A52477.txt".

% The codes this policy decides — outside the section checklist: a claim
% of another policy fails here without failing its own applicability.
% The codes this policy decides: the system and its replacement pads; their
% benefit, durable medical equipment (considered for coverage there).
rule infrared_heating_codes with provenance Policy Article A52477,
        confer "An infrared heating pad system (E0221) consists of a pad or pads containing mechanisms (for example, luminous gallium aluminum arsenide diodes) that generate infrared (or near infrared) light and a power source. Replacement pads are coded A4639":
the policy for code a code is infrared_heating
    if the code is in ["E0221", "A4639"].

section applicability is:

infrared_heating has no specific documentation requirements.

rule infrared_heating_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52477,
        confer "Infrared Heating Pad Systems are considered for coverage under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is infrared_heating.

section question is:

% The LCD covers nothing, applying NCD 270.6: "there are no indications for
% which these devices have been demonstrated to have any therapeutic
% effect". The rule below is this model's device for saying so: it concludes
% a claim reasonable and necessary only for a code in the list of the codes
% the LCD covers, which is empty — so that a claim fails at the question
% (the LCD's denial) and not for want of a rule.
rule infrared_heating_nothing_covered with provenance LCD L33825,
        confer "The device and any related accessories will be denied as not medically reasonable and necessary":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the policy for code the code is infrared_heating
    and the code is in [].
